# boolean-composition-cross-lib root (#189 Slice 0c — cross-library boolean-composition operand)
library "Root".

// A `code is` records concept + a decision force the LocalSource/Interface split (the production KE lane), so
// the composition is exercised at ALL THREE banner-A consumers: the Inferred pivot, the ledger discharge, and
// the Interface façade. "Cross Both" composes a CROSS-LIBRARY total boolean (`"Sib"."Sib Flag"`) with a same-lib
// total boolean ("Root Flag"). In 0b this errored `operand-not-total`; in 0c the family arm proves it total.

concept "Root Records":
- type is Observation.
- shape is RecordSet.
- code is `root-rec`.

concept "Root Flag":
- value type is boolean.
- defined as exists ( "Root Records" ).

concept "Cross Both":
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( "Sib"."Sib Flag" and "Root Flag" ).

// The alias counterexample (disc 465/466): a same-lib scalar-boolean ALIAS to the cross-lib boolean composition
// must AGREE with the composition's bare Boolean form — the legacy alias arm recurses same-layer into "Cross Both",
// whose boolean-comp arm proves it total, so the alias re-exports BARE (never `.satisfied()` a Boolean).
concept "Cross Both Alias":
- value type is boolean.
- defined as "Cross Both".

activity "Refer":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

decision "Triage":
- when "Cross Both" then recommend activity "Refer".
- when "Cross Both Alias" then recommend activity "Refer".
